$DIR/test.p:7:13: enum E: underlying type string must be an integer type
    The type after the enum keyword is the integer type that holds the enum's
    values. It must be an integer type such as uint8 or int32. Leave it out to
    let the compiler pick the smallest one that fits.
    (see "Enums" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.12)
    (run "pluto explain E2303" for a longer explanation)
